          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21327 rustreapi: add a safe data version API",
        "message": "LU-21327 rustreapi: add a safe data version API\n\nrustreapi cannot read a file's data version, which an S3 gateway needs\non every request to tell whether a file changed under it, so the call\nmust cost no more than the ioctl itself.\n\nAdd data_version(), which takes a BorrowedFd and DataVersionFlags\n(ReadFlush, WriteFlush) and makes a single LL_IOC_DATA_VERSION ioctl\nwith no open, stat or allocation.  DataVersionError separates a\ndescriptor that is not a regular file on Lustre (ENOTTY) and one\nopened O_PATH (EBADF) from other errnos.\n\nLL_DV_SZ_UPDATE is left out: the client masks it off this ioctl, so it\nhas never had an effect from user space.\n\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I3fa0efbfa7f918d95ebf04a372bf8aea56dbfe86\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
